# The build context of engine/Dockerfile is the repository root, which also holds tens of GB of
# local data. Send only what the image is built from: the engine's project and source, and the
# web app that builds the chart bundles. Everything else stays out, the data above all (F1 data
# is never baked into an image: the served bundle is mounted at /data).
*
!engine/pyproject.toml
!engine/uv.lock
!engine/README.md
!engine/src/
!web/

# Built or local, inside what is sent: rebuilt in the image, or never shipped.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
engine/src/race_engineer/mcp_server/ui/
web/node_modules/
web/.next/
web/out/
web/public/snapshots/
web/public/saved/
web/coverage/
web/build/
web/.vercel/
web/*.tsbuildinfo
web/next-env.d.ts
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/.DS_Store
